  "make:config": { examples: ["pso make:config storage --service gateway --dry-run","pso make:config storage --service gateway","pso make:config cache --service catalog   # Spring Boot form: a @Configuration class"], effects: ["Orchestrator: writes `src/.app/configs/storage.config.ts`, a plain module whose values are read once when it is first imported. It is used by importing it (from a module controller: `import storageConfig from \"../../../.app/configs/storage.config\"`); the framework neither loads nor injects it.","Spring Boot (layered): writes `infrastructure/config/CacheConfig.java`, a `@Configuration` class found by Spring's component scan like any bean of the service."], checks: ["Framework settings (limits, security, logging, dispatch) are not set here: they live in `pso.config.json` (`pso config:list`)."], failures: ["Generation does not supply secrets: read them from the environment in the generated file, never write them into it."], see: ["concepts/configuration","orchestrator/services-and-providers"] },
